==================================================
ACTUAL BUG
==================================================

pickupBAS correctly does:

    const _pc = findCell(
        atlasLayout,
        p.cell === '6' ? 'ammo' : 'health',
        'idle'
    );

    const _pr = _pc
        ? cellToRect(_pc, SPRITE_SIZE)
        : null;

BUT the actual one-time pickupInit ignores _pr and still emits hardcoded old
32px atlas coordinates:

    const pickupInit = pickups.map((p, n) => {
      const s = 6 + n;
      const tex = p.cell === '6'
        ? `SPRTEX ${s},1,128,0,159,31`
        : `SPRTEX ${s},1,160,0,191,31`;
      return ` ${tex}\n SPRPAL ${s},1,0,1`;
    }).join('\n');

Those coordinates are stale.

They sample:

    ammo:
        p1 x128..159 y0..31

    health:
        p1 x160..191 y0..31

instead of the actual 64x64 cells:

    ammo:
        p1 x320..383 y128..191

    health:
        p1 x384..447 y128..191

This exactly explains the visible hollow/transparent little square.

==================================================
FIX
==================================================

Make pickupInit use the SAME canonical atlas resolution as every other sprite.

Do not hardcode any page/x/y coordinates.

For every pickup:

    const id = p.cell === '6' ? 'ammo' : 'health';
    const c = findCell(atlasLayout, id, 'idle');

If no cell exists:

    log a clear build error
    do not emit a stale fallback texture

If it exists:

    const r = cellToRect(c, SPRITE_SIZE);

emit:

    SPRTEX s,r.page,r.x,r.y,r.x2,r.y2
    SPRPAL s,1,0,1

Conceptually:

    const pickupInit = pickups.map((p, n) => {
      const s = 6 + n;
      const id = p.cell === '6' ? 'ammo' : 'health';
      const c = findCell(atlasLayout, id, 'idle');

      if (!c) {
        console.error('[DOOM] no atlas cell for', id,
                      '— pickup sprite disabled');
        return ` SPROFF ${s}`;
      }

      const r = cellToRect(c, SPRITE_SIZE);

      return [
        ` SPRTEX ${s},${r.page},${r.x},${r.y},${r.x2},${r.y2}`,
        ` SPRPAL ${s},1,0,1`
      ].join('\n');
    }).join('\n');

Use the project's actual rect property names if they are currently x/y/x2/y2
or x/y/y2 etc. Inspect cellToRect first rather than assuming.

==================================================
REMOVE THE DUPLICATED LOOKUP
==================================================

Right now pickupBAS resolves _pc/_pr but does not use _pr for texture setup.

Do not leave two independent pickup texture lookups again.

Prefer one canonical helper, for example:

    resolvePickupRect(p)

or resolve the rect once per pickup while constructing the pickup descriptors.

Then BOTH:

    pickupBAS
    pickupInit

consume that resolved object.

Example intermediate structure:

    pickupsResolved = pickups.map((p,n) => ({
        ...p,
        spriteId: 6+n,
        resourceId: p.cell === '6' ? 'ammo' : 'health',
        rect: ...
    }))

Then use:

    pickupResolved.rect

everywhere.

The important invariant:

    semantic resource
        ->
    findCell
        ->
    cellToRect
        ->
    ALL generated SPRTEX commands

No duplicate hardcoded atlas knowledge.

==================================================
DO NOT KEEP THE OLD FALLBACK
==================================================

Do not fall back to:

    128,0,159,31

or:

    160,0,191,31

Those are obsolete 32px coordinates and hide layout failures.

If resolution fails:

    fail loudly
    or disable that sprite

Never silently sample some unrelated atlas region.

